<task id="195" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Applying a Dataverse email template fills Subject and body with finished text (no XSL, no CDATA debris); Email documents Summary shows the summary once, not raw JSON</title>
    <phase>12 Create-wizard lookups and composer (185 dev check fixes)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>in-progress</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api; modifies .cs and .tsx code.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Two located defects with clear references (the template's own rendered columns or the Dataverse InstantiateTemplate action; summarizeService's existing result normaliser).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>185-fixes</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches DocumentEmailWizard.tsx, which 194 also modifies. Run 194 and 195 one after the other; 193 is independent.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, frontend, react, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Owner 185 dev check C1 (2026-11-16; notes/task-185-notes.md): in Email documents, applying a Dataverse email template put raw XSL (`&lt;?xml version="1.0" ?&gt;&lt;xsl:stylesheet …`) in Subject and left `]]&gt;` debris in the body ("Dear ]]&gt;Valued Customer", a trailing `]]&gt;`); the email that was sent carried that debris. The Summary step showed the playbook's raw JSON (`{"tldr":…,"summary":…,"confidence":0.9}`), twice. Both predate the 178–188 work (other areas' code), but they are user-visible in every composer host this project wired, and a bad email went out. Owner approved the fix 2026-11-16 ("All three").</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in ASP.NET Core minimal APIs, Dataverse email templates, React and the @spaarke/ui-components EmailComposer and DocumentEmailWizard.</role>
  <goal>(1) `POST /api/communications/template/render` returns a plain subject and an HTML body with every Dataverse placeholder resolved (from the regarding record when given, else the placeholder's fallback text, else empty), never XSL and never CDATA markers. (2) The DocumentEmailWizard Summary step shows the summary text (tldr and summary) once, parsed from the playbook output, and falls back to the raw text only when the output is not JSON.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>
- Template render: CommunicationTemplateEndpoints.cs (`/api/communications/template/render`, ~line 50) → EmailTemplateService.cs (Services/Ai/Delivery). It reads the template's `subject` and `body` columns (~141), which on Dataverse are XSL stylesheets with CDATA sections, and only rewrites `{!x}` to `{{x}}` (~182-232). The template rows on dev also carry `subjectsafehtml` / `safehtml` (rendered HTML) with placeholders like `{!account:name;Valued Customer}` (entity:attribute;fallback). Fix options, in order of preference: Dataverse `InstantiateTemplate` (TemplateId, ObjectType, ObjectId) when a regarding record is given and the template's type matches it — called AS THE CALLER, exactly like the route's existing reads; otherwise render from `subjectsafehtml`/`safehtml`, substituting each placeholder from the regarding record if readable, else its fallback, else empty. Check what other callers of IEmailTemplateService / ComposeTemplateSource expect before changing the output shape; if Compose depends on the `{{x}}` tokens, keep that path and fix only the email render.
- Client handler: createXrmEmailComposeHandlers.ts ~348-374 (`onRenderEmailTemplate`) calls the route; every composer host uses it (Console Send Email included — ConversationPane.tsx ~923-926), so the server fix covers them all. The owner reported the Console template "working"; check it against a template with placeholders.
- Summary: DocumentEmailWizard.tsx ~818-835 appends every stream `chunk.content` and renders the concatenation verbatim (~900). The `/api/ai/analysis/execute` stream (AnalysisEndpoints.cs ~652-658) sends the streamed tokens and then the completed node text, both as `chunk` events — hence twice. Fix on the client only (other consumers read that stream): take the last complete JSON object and show `tldr` and `summary`, reusing summarizeService.ts `normalizeResult` (~137; export it or move it to a shared util — do not copy it). Do not change the BFF stream.
- Line numbers are at origin/master `ce6c241964`; re-grep before editing.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Delivery/EmailTemplateService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationTemplateEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DocumentEmailWizard/DocumentEmailWizard.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SummarizeFilesWizard/summarizeService.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/createXrmEmailComposeHandlers.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Delivery/ComposeTemplateSource.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Every change this task makes to Sprk.Bff.Api follows .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md. No new endpoint, DI registration or package. Measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build and record it in the task notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11 / D-66">The fix extends EmailTemplateService; no new service, resolver class or interface. No new core code in Services/Ai beyond this existing class.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 / D-15">Template and regarding-record reads (and InstantiateTemplate, if used) run as the caller, the same as the route today. Never an app-only read for placeholder values.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The route's authorization (CommunicationRecordAuthorizationFilter: Read on the regarding record; template readable by the caller) is unchanged. A placeholder whose value the caller cannot read renders its fallback or empty, never an error that leaks the value's existence.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The render never fails the composer: if a template cannot be rendered, the route returns its existing refusal shape and the composer keeps the user's text.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in the acceptance criteria; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the task notes. No numeric test target. Never run the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests; filter on the touched classes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No deploy in this task. The BFF part reaches dev only through uac-r2's next dev BFF build (project CLAUDE.md §5); the client part through the next PCF/code-page deploy (owner go, D-126).</constraint>
  </constraints>
