  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the render route, EmailTemplateService and every caller of IEmailTemplateService/ComposeTemplateSource; read the dev template shape (subject/body XSL, subjectsafehtml/safehtml, placeholder syntax) from a test fixture or the docs, not a live write.</step>
    <step order="2">Change the email render to produce finished subject and body as in the goal; keep any Compose-only token path unchanged.</step>
    <step order="3">In DocumentEmailWizard, parse the summary stream with the shared normaliser and show tldr and summary once; fall back to the raw text for non-JSON output.</step>
    <step order="4">Write the tests in the acceptance criteria; run them filtered, `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/`, `dotnet test tests/Spaarke.ArchTests`, the touched client folders' suites, `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` and `node scripts/quality/client-lint/client-lint.mjs check`. Record the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="5">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md status to `✅ [done]` AND this POML's status to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 -Project spaarke-ontology-platform-r1`. Record deviations in notes/task-195-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF test: a template whose subject column is an XSL stylesheet renders a plain subject with no `&lt;?xml`, `xsl:` or `]]&gt;` text.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF test: a body placeholder `{!account:name;Valued Customer}` renders the regarding record's value when given and readable, else "Valued Customer"; a placeholder with no fallback and no value renders empty. No `]]&gt;` or `&lt;![CDATA[` remains in the body.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF test: when the caller cannot read the regarding record's attribute, the placeholder renders its fallback and the route still returns 200.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF test: an unrenderable template returns the route's existing refusal shape (no 500); authorization behaviour of the route is unchanged (existing filter tests pass).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Any existing Compose template behaviour is unchanged (existing ComposeTemplateSource / Compose tests pass).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Client test: a summary stream of token chunks followed by the same completed JSON shows the tldr and summary once, with no JSON braces or field names; a non-JSON stream shows its text once.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">summarizeService keeps its behaviour (existing tests pass) after the normaliser is shared.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build clean; ArchTests pass; publish-size delta recorded; tsc and the client-lint ratchet pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If InstantiateTemplate cannot run as the caller, or the safehtml columns are absent for some template types, STOP and report the options before choosing.</trigger>
    <trigger>If another consumer depends on the current `{{x}}` output of the email render, STOP and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Template and summary">
      <steps>
        <step>Semantic Search → Email documents: check the Summary step; on Compose, apply a template with placeholders; send to yourself</step>
        <step>Console → Send Email: apply the same template</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Summary shows readable text once. Subject and body show finished text, no XSL or ]]&gt;; the received email matches.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build the BFF; filtered dotnet test on the touched classes; ArchTests</tool>
    <tool name="npm">jest, tsc and ESLint in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components</tool>
  </tools>
  <execution>
